OL,3,GNEWSAI'm still in pain after being
OL,4,Apossessed by a ghost
OL,5,
OL,6,FAccording to Dr Katy Soar, senior
OL,7,Flecturer in Classical Archaeology at
OL,8,Fthe University of Winchester, the
OL,9,Fearliest recorded haunted house story
OL,10,Fdates to 100- 109CE, when Roman writer
OL,11,FPliny the Younger recounted the tale of
OL,12,Fa Greek philosopher who rented a house
OL,13,Fwith a shackled and howling ghost of an
OL,14,Fold man.
OL,16,FPaul Cowneadow, from Gloucester, says
OL,17,Fhe still suffers from pain caused by a
OL,18,Fghost which attacked and possessed him
OL,19,Fin an old prison.
